#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD9726 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "The sister half of the FDA-SD1124 pair (minted 2026-09-11, M7/T1-11). LBREASND is not in the dataset (None satisfied) while rows 1 and 2 report LBSTAT='NOT DONE', so the remaining condition holds on two rows. Sensitivity is Dataset, so the absence is reported ONCE although both rows qualify. Same dataset shape as the parent's skipped_no_reasnd_column scenario: the parent skips, this rule reports. The SENDIG twin CDISC-SEND-0280 has its own sister, CDISC-SEND-9437. Clean 2-1: no presence rule for --REASND exists anywhere in the corpus, and measured, NO domain in any shipped SDTMIG or SENDIG defines --STAT without also defining --REASND, so no dataset can fire this sister structurally."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBSTAT   type=Char label="Completion Status"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB  | NOT DONE
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | GLUC | NOT DONE
